A when that reads an optional source field. Nothing proves the condition
evaluates when the field is absent, so it is refused; a condition may test
the field's presence. Reading it under a presence test is for the slice that proves
computed expressions.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name:   string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name:  string
	count: int
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	v1_0: {
		count: orelse(v0_0.count, 0)
	}
	lacunas: {
		count: [{
			type:    PrecisionLoss
			message: "counts above 1000 are rounded downstream"
			when:    v0_0.count != _|_ && v0_0.count > 1000
		}]
	}
}
-- out/error --
count is optional in 0.0, and a condition reading an optional field is not supported yet; a condition may test its presence: v0_0.count != _|_:
    1.0.thema:15:34
